<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sumper (2002) & Lenoci-Camp (2008) hierarchical Cahn-Hilliard diatom biosilica phase separation — Code-to-model traceability: 60/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Basic module docstring cites Sumper (2002) and Lenoci & Camp (2008), but functions lack explicit equation mappings and references to the Lean 4 theorems in `morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_071_diatom_frustule_phase_sep.lean`." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py L27–L82: Functions lack explicit paper section/equation and Lean 4 theorem cross-references <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/HEAD/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py#L27-L82>" ;
    pk:hasScore 6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sumper (2002) & Lenoci-Camp (2008) hierarchical Cahn-Hilliard diatom biosilica phase separation — Model fidelity to source: 58/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Integrates the 2D periodic Cahn-Hilliard equation with exact zero-mode Fourier mass conservation (L27-57), separating off-critical droplet (phi0=-0.30) and critical bicontinuous (phi0=0.00) morphologies. However, v1 simulates only a single-scale quench without Lenoci & Camp's (2008) two-stage hierarchical solidification inside primary pores, omits the analytical spinodal dispersion relation sigma(k) = M*k^2*(1 - 3*phi0^2 - eps^2*k^2), and includes no negative control outside the spinodal boundary (|phi0| > 1/sqrt(3))." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py L27–L57: Single-stage 2D spectral Cahn-Hilliard solver without two-stage hierarchical cribrum quench or spinodal dispersion <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/HEAD/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py#L27-L57>" ;
    pk:hasScore 5.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sumper (2002) & Lenoci-Camp (2008) hierarchical Cahn-Hilliard diatom biosilica phase separation — Morphometric validation: 48/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Computes integer-binned 2D radial PSD peak `k_bin` and connected-component pore count (L60-82), yielding discrete quantization error (lambda* = 19.2 px at k_bin=5 vs analytical 15.60 px), and omits sub-bin parabolic interpolation, 6-fold hexatic bond-orientational order |psi_6|, and empirical SEM pore diameter/pitch comparison." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py L60–L82: Integer-binned radial PSD peak without sub-bin interpolation or hexatic |psi_6| <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/HEAD/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py#L60-L82>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-measurement-cahn-hilliard-conserved-mean-order-parameter-phi>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-measurement-cahn-hilliard-primary-droplet-pore-count>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-measurement-cahn-hilliard-primary-droplet-wavelength-lambda> ;
    pk:hasScore 4.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sumper (2002) & Lenoci-Camp (2008) hierarchical Cahn-Hilliard diatom biosilica phase separation — MorphoEval overall 47.7/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 (v1) baseline evaluation of `2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py` (consensus score 51.6/100). The v1 script integrates the fourth-order Cahn-Hilliard PDE d(phi)/dt = M*laplacian(phi^3 - phi - eps^2*laplacian(phi)) via semi-implicit Fourier spectral stepping for off-critical droplet (phi0=-0.30) and critical bicontinuous (phi0=0.00) regimes, but omits two-stage hierarchical quenching (foramen -> cribrum -> cribrella), linear spinodal dispersion sigma(k), outside-spinodal negative controls, parameter sweeps across interfacial length epsilon, and computer-vision segmentation of the *Coscinodiscus wailesii* SEM specimen micrograph. Overall 47.7/100 (faithfulness 41.0, reproducibility 63.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit HEAD; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 58, Morphological realism / specimen match 22, Parameter expressivity 44, Morphometric validation 48, Source and data traceability 62, Code-to-model traceability 60, Reproducibility package 67. Output judged: docs/media/diatom_frustule_phase_sep_comparison.png: rendered output of 2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py at HEAD, image/png, 90542 B, 1400×644 px, artifact_sha256 3d96e9137cd584b0d14db9fdf6c4d8faf5fa1f38fe5885068eb362813098d929 (sha256 3d96e9137cd584b0d14db9fdf6c4d8faf5fa1f38fe5885068eb362813098d929), spec_fingerprint cb843885a61dd35079ecc44f25b12a884b513caa2c4f708fa015d81046e64d1c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: cb843885a61dd35079ecc44f25b12a884b513caa2c4f708fa015d81046e64d1c; artifact_sha256: 3d96e9137cd584b0d14db9fdf6c4d8faf5fa1f38fe5885068eb362813098d929; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/diatom_frustule_phase_sep/coscinodiscus_diatom_specimen.jpg=47aca39b720b67b1..., datasets/diatom_frustule_phase_sep/diatom_frustule_phase_sep_reference.json=558186dc4409fb21..., datasets/diatom_frustule_phase_sep/scout_manifest.json=0eea5a04552420e8...}." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Implement Lenoci & Camp (2008) two-stage quenched hierarchical Cahn-Hilliard phase separation (primary foramen walls at eps_1=1.50 followed by secondary cribrum pore quench at eps_2=0.65 inside unsolidified primary pores) plus Sumper (2002) 3-tier scaling (foramen -> cribrum -> cribrella).",
        "remediation needed: Implement the exact linear spinodal dispersion relation sigma(k) = M*k^2*(1 - 3*phi0^2 - eps^2*k^2), critical wavenumber k_c, and an outside-spinodal negative control (phi0 = -0.65, |phi0| > 1/sqrt(3)) proving homogeneous stability.",
        "remediation needed: Load and SHA-256-verify `datasets/diatom_frustule_phase_sep/diatom_frustule_phase_sep_reference.json` and `coscinodiscus_diatom_specimen.jpg` at runtime, and segment both the primary hexagonal foramen lattice (139 pores, pitch, diameter-to-pitch ratio, hexatic |psi_6|) and secondary cribrum pores (74 pores) from the real *Coscinodiscus wailesii* SEM micrograph.",
        "remediation needed: Upgrade spectral morphometrics to sub-bin parabolic wavenumber interpolation, run a 5-point interfacial-scale parameter sweep across epsilon in {0.75, 1.00, 1.25, 1.50, 1.75}, expose full CLI flags, and render a comprehensive multi-panel synthesis figure and animated hierarchical growth GIF." ;
    pk:hasScore 4.77e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sumper (2002) & Lenoci-Camp (2008) hierarchical Cahn-Hilliard diatom biosilica phase separation — Parameter expressivity: 44/100" ;
